WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.432 --> 00:00:17.105
All right, gentlemen...

2
00:00:18.309 --> 00:00:20.687
Right here is
Black Rock Mountain, men.

3
00:00:20.895 --> 00:00:22.613
Fifteen to twenty minutes ago,

4
00:00:22.814 --> 00:00:26.819
Alpha Coy, became engaged
by 50 to 100 fighters,

5
00:00:27.027 --> 00:00:29.997
up, around, and on the vicinity
of Black Rock mountain.

6
00:00:30.196 --> 00:00:34.292
They're also taking some indirect
fires from this location.

7
00:00:34.492 --> 00:00:37.871
They hope to have them, uh,
backstopped by Bravo Coy

8
00:00:38.079 --> 00:00:40.207
and compress the enemy
between the two of 'em,

9
00:00:40.415 --> 00:00:43.009
setting the conditions
for us to come in

10
00:00:43.209 --> 00:00:44.381
and do our air assault.

11
00:01:05.148 --> 00:01:07.116
What's our
plan for this evening?

12
00:01:07.317 --> 00:01:09.795
Basically, we're rolling in with
the attack of the Command Element

13
00:01:09.819 --> 00:01:12.072
in order to secure
a, uh, high-traffic region

14
00:01:12.280 --> 00:01:13.907
for the, uh...
The Taliban.

15
00:01:23.583 --> 00:01:26.177
So you'll be with
Command Element in a Black Hawk

16
00:01:26.377 --> 00:01:28.189
and I'll be up with
the Joe's in a Chinook, yeah?

17
00:01:28.213 --> 00:01:30.341
Absolutely. Yeah, you get
the better spot, though.

18
00:01:44.145 --> 00:01:46.694
Beck Becks. I actually
have an L-10-11 going out.

19
00:01:46.856 --> 00:01:48.950
Upper foresight is good.

20
00:01:49.150 --> 00:01:50.950
Internals are incomplete.

21
00:01:53.113 --> 00:01:54.956
30 mag, all cooling.

22
00:01:55.156 --> 00:01:58.080
- You can go ahead, over.
- Roger, work it off.

23
00:02:07.335 --> 00:02:11.841
Arrow 2-5, I have
contact on all friendlies.

24
00:02:12.048 --> 00:02:14.676
We have good situational awareness.

25
00:02:31.442 --> 00:02:33.160
Arrow's clear.

26
00:02:33.361 --> 00:02:35.159
- Plug it in.
- Yep, Roger.

27
00:03:01.514 --> 00:03:03.714
Truckade...
Her movement's the tree line.

28
00:03:04.767 --> 00:03:06.940
- Got anybody in there?
- I'm looking, sir.

29
00:03:10.648 --> 00:03:12.525
Right there,
clock him, hold on a second.

30
00:03:12.734 --> 00:03:14.134
Oh, shit, right.

31
00:03:14.277 --> 00:03:17.121
Arrow 2-5, we
have multiple enemies

32
00:03:17.322 --> 00:03:19.199
in trees, engaging west of road.

33
00:03:24.120 --> 00:03:25.997
Ah, we're getting shot at.

34
00:03:27.457 --> 00:03:29.926
- Roger...
- Oh, shit, their in...

35
00:03:30.126 --> 00:03:33.005
That's affirmative.
We are taking fire

36
00:03:33.213 --> 00:03:35.056
from the west side...

37
00:03:35.256 --> 00:03:37.384
And, Hard Rock, this is Arrow,

38
00:03:37.592 --> 00:03:39.845
we need permission
to engage the tree line,

39
00:03:40.053 --> 00:03:41.475
where the RPG came from.

40
00:03:41.638 --> 00:03:44.187
Roger, you're clear to engage.

41
00:03:44.390 --> 00:03:47.269
Uh, fucking
light that tree line up, hit it.

42
00:03:47.477 --> 00:03:50.196
Roger.

43
00:03:50.396 --> 00:03:52.148
- Just to the left. Hit it.
- Roger.

44
00:03:54.150 --> 00:03:56.994
Okay, make
sure that-Okay, looking good.

45
00:03:57.195 --> 00:03:59.163
- Oh, shit.
- Hit it, hit it.

46
00:03:59.364 --> 00:04:00.924
- RPG right over there.
- Right, hit it!

47
00:04:01.032 --> 00:04:03.751
We have multiple
RPGs coming from that side

48
00:04:03.952 --> 00:04:05.829
at the aircraft, I copy.

49
00:04:15.838 --> 00:04:18.682
Right, hit it.

50
00:04:18.883 --> 00:04:21.352
Hit it again.

51
00:04:21.552 --> 00:04:23.429
Hit it again.

52
00:04:29.018 --> 00:04:30.645
Good man, good man.

53
00:04:30.853 --> 00:04:33.072
We neutralized the one RPG site.

54
00:04:33.273 --> 00:04:35.446
Roger, that's good, copy.

55
00:04:35.650 --> 00:04:37.823
- Come up the road.
- Up the road, Roger.

56
00:04:38.027 --> 00:04:39.713
Up the road, up the road
to the left... to the left.

57
00:04:39.737 --> 00:04:41.674
- Right there in that building.
- Arrow 2-5, are you seeing

58
00:04:41.698 --> 00:04:43.245
- or we're taking more contact?
- Okay.

59
00:04:43.449 --> 00:04:45.076
Roger, we're engaged.

60
00:04:45.285 --> 00:04:47.458
Oh my god, I got a bucket.

61
00:04:47.662 --> 00:04:50.256
Oh, shit...

62
00:04:51.624 --> 00:04:53.046
On, shit.

63
00:05:20.903 --> 00:05:24.157
2-5, 2-5, one
of our vehicles got hit.

64
00:05:24.365 --> 00:05:27.084
We lost the line of...

65
00:05:33.249 --> 00:05:35.047
Standby, we're
missing friendlies.

66
00:05:35.251 --> 00:05:36.691
We're trying to
get him out of there.

67
00:06:01.110 --> 00:06:03.283
There was a huge,
huge air assault operation.

68
00:06:03.446 --> 00:06:06.575
This was involving
the first and 5-0-8,

69
00:06:06.783 --> 00:06:09.252
the parachute infantry
regiment, an entire regiment.

70
00:06:09.452 --> 00:06:12.205
It was involving
7th Special Forces Group,

71
00:06:12.413 --> 00:06:14.791
more than 15
different air assets.

72
00:06:14.999 --> 00:06:17.172
It was a huge operation,

73
00:06:17.377 --> 00:06:19.817
and it was going to be going on
for weeks and weeks and weeks,

74
00:06:19.879 --> 00:06:22.348
and within that first hour,

75
00:06:22.548 --> 00:06:24.028
one of the Chinooks
had been shot down

76
00:06:24.217 --> 00:06:25.935
by a Taliban
Surface-to-Air missile.

77
00:06:27.512 --> 00:06:29.606
They had to try
to secure this huge,

78
00:06:29.806 --> 00:06:31.308
flaming crash site,

79
00:06:31.474 --> 00:06:33.394
and they didn't know
if there were any survivors.

80
00:06:33.518 --> 00:06:35.816
What happened
when you touched down?

81
00:06:36.020 --> 00:06:37.988
We had heard that
there had been a Chinook

82
00:06:38.189 --> 00:06:39.669
that was shot down,
but I just focused

83
00:06:39.816 --> 00:06:41.989
on my job of shooting video

84
00:06:42.151 --> 00:06:43.949
and trying to get the story.

85
00:07:07.468 --> 00:07:09.345
1-3-6, over.

86
00:07:14.434 --> 00:07:16.107
Air Humvee.

87
00:07:34.454 --> 00:07:38.049
Roger, we heard there was a downed
aircraft. Can we confirm that?

88
00:07:47.467 --> 00:07:49.219
Is anybody looking
to our North route?

89
00:08:11.157 --> 00:08:12.909
I'd linked up
with the Commander,

90
00:08:13.075 --> 00:08:14.577
Lieutenant Colonel Brian Menace.

91
00:08:14.744 --> 00:08:16.462
And we were moving
to clear a compound

92
00:08:16.662 --> 00:08:18.164
so he'd have a secure location

93
00:08:18.372 --> 00:08:21.342
because they needed
to control 15 aircraft

94
00:08:21.542 --> 00:08:23.510
that were racked
and stacked in the sky.

95
00:08:28.633 --> 00:08:31.352
This had now become a combat
search-and-rescue mission

96
00:08:31.552 --> 00:08:33.600
in addition to the ongoing
offensive operation.

97
00:08:44.649 --> 00:08:46.071
Spread out.

98
00:08:59.914 --> 00:09:02.167
- Moo.
- I need to get by you.

99
00:09:02.375 --> 00:09:03.797
Do you speak English?

100
00:09:04.001 --> 00:09:05.298
Hey, he does.

101
00:09:15.930 --> 00:09:18.479
Hey, get him over here now.

102
00:09:21.644 --> 00:09:24.238
Get him over here now.
Get him out here.

103
00:09:30.570 --> 00:09:31.913
Come on.

104
00:09:37.577 --> 00:09:40.171
Let me see it.
Here, all right.

105
00:09:43.708 --> 00:09:45.548
Yeah, these guys check out.
They're friendlies.

106
00:09:53.718 --> 00:09:55.140
Thank you.

107
00:09:55.344 --> 00:09:56.846
Who the fuck is our...

108
00:10:22.705 --> 00:10:24.600
- All right, you guys ready?
- Yeah.

109
00:10:24.624 --> 00:10:25.664
Which contact...

110
00:10:25.750 --> 00:10:27.728
- That one right there.
- Okay.

111
00:10:27.752 --> 00:10:30.551
Up, up, right there.
Hit it.

112
00:10:30.713 --> 00:10:32.056
Roger.

113
00:10:35.384 --> 00:10:36.977
Take that, fucker.
Here we go.

114
00:10:37.178 --> 00:10:38.680
- Coming up left.
- Roger.

115
00:10:38.888 --> 00:10:40.561
We nailed the shit
out of that one.

116
00:10:48.689 --> 00:10:50.487
Hey, Jimbo, what are we hearing?

117
00:11:01.577 --> 00:11:03.079
Thank you.

118
00:11:06.874 --> 00:11:08.717
I think what's
important to remember

119
00:11:08.918 --> 00:11:10.886
with this huge
operation is that...

120
00:11:11.087 --> 00:11:12.885
And it was an operation
that still went on

121
00:11:13.089 --> 00:11:14.386
for weeks and weeks thereafter.

122
00:11:14.590 --> 00:11:17.309
And there were many
battles that still followed

123
00:11:17.510 --> 00:11:21.265
and towns that these troops
had to clear, and...

124
00:11:22.640 --> 00:11:25.314
but the important thing that...
That can't get lost in this

125
00:11:25.518 --> 00:11:27.486
is that seven souls were lost.

126
00:11:27.687 --> 00:11:30.156
The five crew of the flipper

127
00:11:30.356 --> 00:11:32.154
and our coalition partners,

128
00:11:32.358 --> 00:11:34.577
a Brit and a Canadian...

129
00:11:34.777 --> 00:11:37.280
And that it... it
made no difference

130
00:11:37.488 --> 00:11:40.412
that... that it
was internationals

131
00:11:40.616 --> 00:11:42.243
or that they
might be reporters...

132
00:11:42.451 --> 00:11:45.045
That we had Americans that
were willing to risk their lives

133
00:11:45.246 --> 00:11:47.795
and go after and make sure
to recover the fallen.

134
00:12:05.766 --> 00:12:08.144
They had to count
the bodies of the fallen.

135
00:12:08.310 --> 00:12:12.611
And when I tracked down
Sergeant Greg Strickland,

136
00:12:12.815 --> 00:12:14.863
whose little six-man platoon...

137
00:12:15.067 --> 00:12:17.240
He had gone in there
and had counted five bodies.

138
00:12:17.445 --> 00:12:19.698
And he thought, okay,
well, I found the crew.

139
00:12:19.905 --> 00:12:22.249
And he was ordered
over the radio

140
00:12:22.450 --> 00:12:24.077
to go back in and
count the bodies again

141
00:12:24.285 --> 00:12:26.003
because the reporters
are missing.

142
00:12:26.203 --> 00:12:29.127
And he told me on camera
that he went back in there

143
00:12:29.331 --> 00:12:31.083
to look for the reporters,

144
00:12:31.292 --> 00:12:33.590
and he said he...
That... to look for me.

145
00:12:33.794 --> 00:12:35.554
I didn't know I was
supposed to be on that...

146
00:12:35.671 --> 00:12:37.548
On that helicopter,
on that Chinook.

147
00:12:37.757 --> 00:12:40.055
It was the guys
who told me afterwards.

148
00:12:41.552 --> 00:12:42.678
It was a punch to the gut

149
00:12:42.845 --> 00:12:46.224
because it was
this realization that...

150
00:12:48.809 --> 00:12:52.655
men put their lives at risk
to come after reporters,

151
00:12:52.855 --> 00:12:54.653
to come after people like me,

152
00:12:54.857 --> 00:12:56.905
even though I'm
not a service member.

153
00:12:57.943 --> 00:12:59.536
It's not that I have a purpose,

154
00:12:59.695 --> 00:13:02.369
but it's that I have
this huge responsibility.

155
00:13:02.573 --> 00:13:04.496
I have a debt to
pay back to these guys.

156
00:13:04.700 --> 00:13:06.043
I have to tell their stories.

157
00:13:06.243 --> 00:13:09.713
Did you stay embedded
with this group

158
00:13:09.914 --> 00:13:12.167
for the entirety
of their mission?

159
00:13:12.374 --> 00:13:16.504
No, I... I was with them
for a good week or so

160
00:13:16.712 --> 00:13:18.714
and then it was time
for me to dis-embed.

161
00:13:18.881 --> 00:13:21.760
I was trying to get in with the
Special Forces Teams in Iraq

162
00:13:21.967 --> 00:13:24.766
and I had a hit date
to try to get in there.

163
00:13:24.970 --> 00:13:27.849
And so it was time for me
to hitchhike my way to Iraq.

164
00:13:33.145 --> 00:13:35.694
I went to Diyala province,

165
00:13:35.898 --> 00:13:38.117
which is the size
of Massachusetts

166
00:13:38.317 --> 00:13:39.910
along the Iranian border,

167
00:13:40.069 --> 00:13:41.669
because that's where
I was going to embed

168
00:13:41.862 --> 00:13:44.866
with the Operational
Detachment Alpha 0-7-2.

169
00:13:46.116 --> 00:13:49.541
O.D.A 0-7-2 was
a so-called rough team...

170
00:13:49.745 --> 00:13:52.919
Very austere, out there
on the fringe of the empire...

171
00:13:53.123 --> 00:13:56.252
Where every day was truly
a fight for survival.

172
00:13:56.418 --> 00:13:58.261
Even their Special
Forces Commander

173
00:13:58.462 --> 00:14:00.681
called these twelve men
hard-charging

174
00:14:00.881 --> 00:14:03.009
and living the Special
Forces Dream...

175
00:14:04.093 --> 00:14:06.437
but they'd just lost
one of their own,

176
00:14:06.595 --> 00:14:10.145
Rob Pirelli, who I knew
from an earlier SF mission.

177
00:14:13.853 --> 00:14:16.606
Tell me... um...
tell me about Rob.

178
00:14:16.772 --> 00:14:19.571
Rob was the
senior engineer on our team.

179
00:14:19.775 --> 00:14:22.119
- He...
- Which means what? What does an engineer do?

180
00:14:22.319 --> 00:14:24.617
Well, the engineer
is responsible for

181
00:14:24.822 --> 00:14:28.702
anything that
we have to build or destroy,

182
00:14:28.909 --> 00:14:33.130
or... he's responsible for
movement of all our equipment,

183
00:14:33.289 --> 00:14:34.791
accountability for
all our equipment.

184
00:14:34.999 --> 00:14:40.176
Um, basically he's the
logistics expert on the team.

185
00:14:40.379 --> 00:14:45.727
So an engineer-— So building
stuff and also, like, blowing stuff up?

186
00:14:45.926 --> 00:14:48.850
- Yeah.
- Okay, so, but building stuff too

187
00:14:49.054 --> 00:14:50.532
because I think a lot
of folks don't understand

188
00:14:50.556 --> 00:14:52.436
- that you guys do all sorts of things.
- Right.

189
00:14:52.558 --> 00:14:53.935
When we moved into this outpost,

190
00:14:54.143 --> 00:14:56.111
it was a house,
basically in desert,

191
00:14:56.312 --> 00:14:58.314
surrounded by barbed-wire fence.

192
00:14:58.480 --> 00:15:02.075
Within a month,
Rob had built the camp.

193
00:15:19.335 --> 00:15:23.715
♪ This ain't no world
for the weary eyed

194
00:15:23.923 --> 00:15:28.520
♪ This ain't no game
for the foolish child

195
00:15:28.719 --> 00:15:30.687
♪ This ain't no place

196
00:15:30.846 --> 00:15:33.099
♪ Got to fall in line

197
00:15:33.307 --> 00:15:38.438
- ♪ Gone awry...
- He did everything from install the protective barriers

198
00:15:38.646 --> 00:15:40.819
to running electricity
for the house,

199
00:15:41.023 --> 00:15:42.900
repairing generators.

200
00:15:46.946 --> 00:15:49.574
He was literally working
until he went to bed.

201
00:15:49.782 --> 00:15:52.456
He'd wake up in the middle of the
night to play some online poker,

202
00:15:52.660 --> 00:15:54.879
go back to sleep,
wake up in the morning,

203
00:15:55.079 --> 00:15:56.473
still in his AC-Which
and his boots,

204
00:15:56.497 --> 00:15:58.716
ready to work in the morning
with a smile on his face.

205
00:15:58.916 --> 00:16:01.965
We thought it appropriate
to name the camp after him

206
00:16:02.169 --> 00:16:04.718
since he did so much
of that work on his own.

207
00:16:22.106 --> 00:16:24.084
We've been kinda holding
off on this one a little bit,

208
00:16:24.108 --> 00:16:27.282
but let's talk about
Rob and about that day.

209
00:16:27.486 --> 00:16:30.786
Yeah, it's a difficult
subject to talk about,

210
00:16:30.990 --> 00:16:33.994
but any questions you want
answered, you want to...

211
00:16:34.201 --> 00:16:36.750
find out about it, I'm more
than happy to talk about it.

212
00:16:36.954 --> 00:16:39.377
Bring us-— Let's
walk through that day.

213
00:16:46.880 --> 00:16:48.507
We drove out there,

214
00:16:48.716 --> 00:16:50.684
in an area
we've never been before.

215
00:16:50.884 --> 00:16:53.933
There was the makings
of a small village

216
00:16:54.138 --> 00:16:55.731
and so we stopped.

217
00:17:00.269 --> 00:17:04.365
My gunner, he had told me that he
saw somebody on top of the roof,

218
00:17:04.565 --> 00:17:06.408
somebody who was
wearing all black.

219
00:17:06.608 --> 00:17:09.045
And he had an AK, and he was
running around on top of the roof.

220
00:17:09.069 --> 00:17:11.197
The compound
directly to your North,

221
00:17:11.405 --> 00:17:13.954
we have one individual
up on the roof.

222
00:17:14.158 --> 00:17:15.876
And he had seen people

223
00:17:16.076 --> 00:17:17.953
maneuvering towards
his building,

224
00:17:18.162 --> 00:17:20.256
and he was sporadically
firing his weapon

225
00:17:20.456 --> 00:17:21.673
from off the top of the roof.

226
00:17:27.838 --> 00:17:32.435
And they started moving aerial
assets over to our location.

227
00:17:37.014 --> 00:17:39.437
My team Sergeant,

228
00:17:39.641 --> 00:17:42.315
he said "I've been shot,"
you know "Man down, eagle down."

229
00:17:42.519 --> 00:17:44.396
Eagle down!

230
00:17:46.648 --> 00:17:49.197
I directed my medic

231
00:17:49.401 --> 00:17:52.450
to maneuver up to the building
where we thought that he was.

232
00:17:53.572 --> 00:17:55.012
And I looked over to my right

233
00:17:55.199 --> 00:17:59.045
and I saw my Senior Charlie
at the time, Rob.

234
00:17:59.244 --> 00:18:00.791
He was laying on his back.

235
00:18:06.126 --> 00:18:07.766
I just remember reaching
around the corner

236
00:18:07.836 --> 00:18:10.180
and grabbing the strap
on his kit,

237
00:18:10.339 --> 00:18:13.639
and pulling him around
the corner of the building.

238
00:18:15.511 --> 00:18:17.138
It was crazy
because he looked...

239
00:18:17.346 --> 00:18:19.189
Other than the fact
that he was unconscious,

240
00:18:19.348 --> 00:18:21.851
he looked like
nothing was wrong with him.

241
00:18:25.729 --> 00:18:27.402
And then I looked on his helmet,

242
00:18:27.606 --> 00:18:31.076
and there was a... uh, an
entry mark on the helmet

243
00:18:31.276 --> 00:18:33.574
basically the round
and pierced his helmet.

244
00:18:33.779 --> 00:18:36.578
The individual who
shot at Rob and Don,

245
00:18:36.782 --> 00:18:37.982
he was the battalion commander

246
00:18:38.117 --> 00:18:40.586
for all of al-Qaeda
in that area.

247
00:18:40.786 --> 00:18:42.413
So I pulled back the Iraqis

248
00:18:42.621 --> 00:18:44.089
and we used an F16

249
00:18:44.289 --> 00:18:46.542
to do a couple runs
on this objective.

250
