495
00:32:32.909 --> 00:32:35.788
opportunity to say good-bye.

496
00:32:35.995 --> 00:32:38.965
It may give us another opportunity
to meet Rob in a way.

497
00:32:48.216 --> 00:32:50.310
Rob's dad had shared with me

498
00:32:50.510 --> 00:32:52.979
that he was talking to his
Congressman in Massachusetts

499
00:32:53.179 --> 00:32:55.056
to try to go into the war zone

500
00:32:55.264 --> 00:32:57.608
because he wanted to see
the combat outpost...

501
00:32:57.809 --> 00:32:59.356
The house that his son
had built.

502
00:32:59.560 --> 00:33:02.734
And there was no way
that the Congressman

503
00:33:02.939 --> 00:33:05.909
or anybody in the government
was going to let, uh,

504
00:33:06.109 --> 00:33:08.612
somebody go over
and do something like that,

505
00:33:08.820 --> 00:33:09.912
or hopefully not.

506
00:33:10.113 --> 00:33:11.740
So he made me promise

507
00:33:11.906 --> 00:33:13.384
that I would try to get
back over there

508
00:33:13.408 --> 00:33:16.252
and let him know that his son's
outpost was still there,

509
00:33:16.411 --> 00:33:18.664
that his son hadn't
been forgotten over there.

510
00:34:03.166 --> 00:34:05.965
The Green Beret's 10th
Special Forces Group,

511
00:34:06.169 --> 00:34:08.297
they knew that I was
planning to go back

512
00:34:08.504 --> 00:34:11.132
to Iraq with them when they
re-deployed for the second year.

513
00:34:11.299 --> 00:34:13.597
They also knew
that I was injured

514
00:34:13.801 --> 00:34:15.195
and that I had to
come back from the injury

515
00:34:15.219 --> 00:34:17.938
and I would have to prove myself
to them on that one, as well.

516
00:34:19.307 --> 00:34:22.732
I was back with the serious
gunners of ODA 0-9-4.

517
00:34:22.935 --> 00:34:25.905
The "machs gut" guys
who get it done.

518
00:34:26.105 --> 00:34:27.448
- You guys ready?
- Yeah!

519
00:34:27.648 --> 00:34:29.528
All right, on you,
all right, here we go, dudes.

520
00:34:29.609 --> 00:34:31.628
They invited me to
go through their shoot house

521
00:34:31.652 --> 00:34:33.074
with live fire.

522
00:34:43.998 --> 00:34:46.000
Stay in the room!

523
00:35:00.181 --> 00:35:02.400
Hey, what do you guys got?

524
00:35:02.600 --> 00:35:06.070
We bypassed a pool door
on the right in the beginning.

525
00:35:06.270 --> 00:35:08.693
We got a team who's checking it.

526
00:35:08.898 --> 00:35:11.697
Hey, what do you want
for direction of movement?

527
00:35:11.901 --> 00:35:13.448
Where we going, sir?

528
00:35:13.653 --> 00:35:15.621
To the left and back that way.

529
00:35:15.822 --> 00:35:18.325
All right, ready?
All right! Go.

530
00:35:18.533 --> 00:35:21.252
- - Hey, remember,
it's a shotgun door!

531
00:35:21.452 --> 00:35:22.829
Everybody! Hey!

532
00:35:23.037 --> 00:35:26.382
- - Hey, everybody...
There's a closed door on the right.

533
00:35:26.582 --> 00:35:28.050
Closed door, right!

534
00:35:29.877 --> 00:35:31.299
- Everybody good?
- Good.

535
00:35:31.504 --> 00:35:34.053
- Oh, why is that door shut?
- We're moving right behind...

536
00:35:34.257 --> 00:35:35.850
We're moving.

537
00:35:36.050 --> 00:35:37.643
All right,
let's go... let's go.

538
00:35:37.844 --> 00:35:39.471
Ready? Everybody up?
Let's go.

539
00:35:50.439 --> 00:35:51.736
After this training,

540
00:35:51.899 --> 00:35:54.402
I'd been invited
to climb Mt. Rainier

541
00:35:54.610 --> 00:35:56.453
with wounded Special Operators.

542
00:35:56.654 --> 00:35:58.656
This would be the final test

543
00:35:58.865 --> 00:36:03.245
to prove that...
That the ankle was back

544
00:36:03.411 --> 00:36:05.288
and that I could hack it.

545
00:36:09.083 --> 00:36:11.051
On the rope line in front of me

546
00:36:11.252 --> 00:36:14.005
was blind Navy Seal, Lion Joe,

547
00:36:14.213 --> 00:36:17.433
who if you remember
in the American Sniper movie,

548
00:36:17.633 --> 00:36:22.104
he was the one who had been shot
in the face on that rooftop...

549
00:36:24.265 --> 00:36:29.442
And a marine recon scout
who had also been blinded,

550
00:36:29.604 --> 00:36:32.858
and an army soldier
who had lost his legs,

551
00:36:33.065 --> 00:36:38.287
and a ranger who had served in Somalia
in the Black Hawk Down mission,

552
00:36:38.446 --> 00:36:40.289
Kenny Thomas.

553
00:36:42.033 --> 00:36:45.458
And at more than 14,000 feet
at the top of this volcano...

554
00:36:46.913 --> 00:36:50.167
the lesson that I learned
from these Special Operators...

555
00:36:50.374 --> 00:36:52.718
From these wounded warrior
Special Operators,

556
00:36:52.919 --> 00:36:54.592
you don't quit.

557
00:36:54.795 --> 00:36:57.799
And it was that moment that
I was able to prove to myself

558
00:36:58.007 --> 00:36:59.509
that I was back from the injury

559
00:36:59.717 --> 00:37:01.435
and that it was time
to get back to Iraq.

560
00:37:10.478 --> 00:37:12.598
Neither one of you
have ever heard this story.

561
00:37:12.730 --> 00:37:14.152
I'm sure we haven't.

562
00:37:14.315 --> 00:37:16.363
The last Christmas
that Rob was here,

563
00:37:16.567 --> 00:37:20.447
which was, um, 2006,

564
00:37:20.655 --> 00:37:22.828
we went up to Uncle Ralph's
as we always do.

565
00:37:23.032 --> 00:37:25.592
- We go up to Uncle Ralph's for Christmas Eve...
- Christmas Eve.

566
00:37:30.706 --> 00:37:33.175
And opened all the presents.

567
00:37:33.334 --> 00:37:35.052
We do what we always do.

568
00:37:35.253 --> 00:37:38.177
You and dad left early,
and Rob and I stayed.

569
00:37:39.840 --> 00:37:41.842
- Tara, what are you looking at?
- Cosette?

570
00:37:42.051 --> 00:37:44.019
- Robbie.
- Robbie?

571
00:37:44.220 --> 00:37:46.689
When Rob decided
he wanted to leave,

572
00:37:46.889 --> 00:37:49.267
we got in the car
and left Uncle Ralph's.

573
00:37:51.269 --> 00:37:53.897
We were driving home
and it was the moments

574
00:37:54.105 --> 00:37:57.075
that Rob confided in me
for the first time.

575
00:37:57.275 --> 00:38:00.324
It was one of those times
where he just let it all out.

576
00:38:02.363 --> 00:38:04.240
And he told me that

577
00:38:04.490 --> 00:38:07.289
he wasn't necessarily
planning on coming home.

578
00:38:07.493 --> 00:38:10.212
Oh, from Iraq, okay.

579
00:38:10.371 --> 00:38:13.170
So he had an idea in 2006
that he wouldn't be home.

580
00:38:13.374 --> 00:38:14.671
You know Rob.

581
00:38:14.875 --> 00:38:16.752
It doesn't surprise me,
but I didn't...

582
00:38:16.961 --> 00:38:20.306
As a mother, he ain't gonna confide
in me all that stuff anyways,

583
00:38:20.506 --> 00:38:22.224
but I did not know that.

584
00:38:22.425 --> 00:38:24.644
I can remember the last time...

585
00:38:25.970 --> 00:38:28.598
I dropped at the airport.
I saw him that Christmas.

586
00:38:28.806 --> 00:38:31.776
And he says, "You don't
have to hug me."

587
00:38:31.976 --> 00:38:34.104
Until this day, I wish I did.

588
00:38:34.312 --> 00:38:36.155
Well, you don't know.

589
00:38:36.355 --> 00:38:38.232
No, you don't.
You really don't.

590
00:38:46.282 --> 00:38:48.080
It is what it is.

591
00:39:02.840 --> 00:39:04.717
- All right, Bill.
- See you.

592
00:39:08.346 --> 00:39:10.269
Did you have
any idea at that point

593
00:39:10.473 --> 00:39:12.271
how you were gonna figure out

594
00:39:12.475 --> 00:39:13.772
how to get there?

595
00:39:15.102 --> 00:39:17.776
No, I knew I was going
to do whatever it took.

596
00:39:26.238 --> 00:39:28.438
- Oh, there's somebody I know.
- Hey, what's up?

597
00:39:33.371 --> 00:39:35.920
When I re-deployed
with them again,

598
00:39:36.123 --> 00:39:39.343
Rob's team was in
a completely different location

599
00:39:39.543 --> 00:39:42.046
very far from
Combat Outpost Pirelli.

600
00:40:06.570 --> 00:40:10.325
My team we're the elite
unit down here in this province.

601
00:40:10.533 --> 00:40:13.161
We're here to bring
credibility and legitimacy

602
00:40:13.369 --> 00:40:15.246
the Iraqi Security Forces.

603
00:40:15.454 --> 00:40:17.015
- How do you do that?
- Once we get here,

604
00:40:17.039 --> 00:40:19.337
we have to identify
a fit partner,

605
00:40:19.542 --> 00:40:21.260
foreign internal
defense partner.

606
00:40:21.460 --> 00:40:24.384
And the party that we identified
is the an-Nasiriyah SWAT

607
00:40:24.588 --> 00:40:26.090
Special Weapons Attack team.

608
00:40:26.340 --> 00:40:29.184
So we had to select
those operators

609
00:40:29.343 --> 00:40:32.347
that we felt would be
effective in this area

610
00:40:32.513 --> 00:40:35.517
in order to set the conditions
for sustainable security.

611
00:40:35.724 --> 00:40:37.977
Everybody, this on you,

612
00:40:38.185 --> 00:40:39.653
knock out ten push ups...

613
00:40:39.854 --> 00:40:43.700
and then we take a break.

614
00:40:43.858 --> 00:40:45.485
I'm not gonna count for you,

615
00:40:45.693 --> 00:40:47.741
but, you know, if you only
do two, that's on you.

616
00:40:47.945 --> 00:40:50.824
You're not getting any stronger.

617
00:40:51.031 --> 00:40:53.454
Okay, so...

618
00:41:03.502 --> 00:41:05.550
They can do multiple
sets of that as well.

619
00:41:08.299 --> 00:41:11.428
This rotation in an-Nasiriyah
did not get large scale

620
00:41:11.635 --> 00:41:13.103
for on-surge operations.

621
00:41:13.304 --> 00:41:17.525
We're leaving those type of operations
up to the Iraqi Security Forces.

622
00:41:17.725 --> 00:41:20.274
So, you know, the IPs are gonna
do it, the IA are gonna do it.

623
00:41:20.478 --> 00:41:23.573
I think that's
a sign of progress.

624
00:41:23.772 --> 00:41:25.615
I think that's what
we should be doing.

625
00:41:34.116 --> 00:41:36.414
'Ready, guys?
- Yeah! Up!

626
00:41:37.745 --> 00:41:38.871
Keep it up!

627
00:41:44.585 --> 00:41:46.428
Up!

628
00:41:48.214 --> 00:41:49.591
Ahh.

629
00:41:58.599 --> 00:42:01.318
Oh my god, we're doing an excellent
job of teaching jumping jacks.

630
00:42:01.519 --> 00:42:03.237
The excitement and the fun

631
00:42:03.437 --> 00:42:05.405
and you know the things
that they signed up...

632
00:42:05.606 --> 00:42:08.951
- The adrenaline stuff?
- To do or their kind doing,

633
00:42:09.109 --> 00:42:11.111
is kind of going
by the wayside a little bit,

634
00:42:11.278 --> 00:42:15.033
but everybody understands
that that is where we should be,

635
00:42:15.241 --> 00:42:16.538
and that's a good thing.

636
00:42:26.710 --> 00:42:30.260
So difference between
last year and this year?

637
00:42:30.464 --> 00:42:34.344
Last year we had
to walk 500 meters

638
00:42:34.552 --> 00:42:37.021
to go take a shower,

639
00:42:37.221 --> 00:42:41.021
and we were going to the bathroom
in a hole that I dug in the ground.

640
00:42:41.225 --> 00:42:45.025
And this year, I have people
wash and fold my laundry.

641
00:42:45.229 --> 00:42:47.277
Completely different
from last deployment.

642
00:42:49.441 --> 00:42:52.069
Honestly, there's times
where this deployment,

643
00:42:52.278 --> 00:42:55.407
I'd say, man, I wish we were back
up at, you know, COP Pirelli

644
00:42:55.614 --> 00:42:58.834
because... I mean, I definitely
miss Rob every day.

645
00:43:00.619 --> 00:43:02.371
I'd like to go back up.

646
00:43:02.580 --> 00:43:05.129
And it'd just be interesting
to see what it's evolved into,

647
00:43:05.332 --> 00:43:07.551
and just kinda go
back through some memories

648
00:43:07.751 --> 00:43:09.048
from being out there

649
00:43:09.253 --> 00:43:11.847
and kinda walk
those paths again.

650
00:43:38.741 --> 00:43:41.039
When Rob had passed,

651
00:43:41.201 --> 00:43:46.503
my dad, he would go down
to the coffee shop

652
00:43:46.707 --> 00:43:50.052
and grab a coffee
for himself also for Rob.

653
00:43:56.508 --> 00:43:58.977
He would come down
to the cemetery...

654
00:44:00.220 --> 00:44:04.270
and it would be his chance
to sit and talk with Rob.

655
00:44:09.688 --> 00:44:11.531
He would park his car.

656
00:44:11.732 --> 00:44:13.575
He would have a pin in his car

657
00:44:13.776 --> 00:44:15.744
where Rob's picture would be.

658
00:44:20.741 --> 00:44:22.664
And he would walk up

659
00:44:22.868 --> 00:44:25.371
to Rob's resting place...

660
00:44:56.193 --> 00:45:00.824
and he would take a pin
and poke Rob's coffee.

661
00:45:03.450 --> 00:45:06.670
And as it was dripping out,

662
00:45:06.870 --> 00:45:11.376
he would drink
his coffee with Rob.

663
00:45:15.879 --> 00:45:18.632
That was...
That was their time together.

664
00:45:23.804 --> 00:45:29.152
My father passed away
on September 11th, 2012.

665
00:45:29.351 --> 00:45:33.731
He was really sick
and in a hard place,

666
00:45:33.939 --> 00:45:36.863
but he knew it was... okay

667
00:45:37.067 --> 00:45:38.660
because he was gonna
see his son again.

668
00:45:38.819 --> 00:45:42.119
We wanted to have him

669
00:45:42.322 --> 00:45:44.745
buried as close
as we could to Rob

670
00:45:44.950 --> 00:45:47.453
and we know that's what
he would have wanted,

671
00:45:47.661 --> 00:45:49.789
so we made that happen.

672
00:46:02.676 --> 00:46:06.101
Tim, the medic,
who had tried to save

673
00:46:06.305 --> 00:46:08.865
his Green Beret brother and help
him breathe his last breathes...

674
00:46:10.601 --> 00:46:14.401
wanted to know that the
place that Rob had built...

675
00:46:14.605 --> 00:46:16.699
He wanted to know
about the changes there,

676
00:46:16.899 --> 00:46:20.199
but the military P.A.O.s
had said that my...

677
00:46:20.402 --> 00:46:23.622
My embed was with
10th Special Forces Group

678
00:46:23.822 --> 00:46:26.041
and was not with
1st Special Forces Group,

679
00:46:26.241 --> 00:46:27.584
which was now located

680
00:46:27.785 --> 00:46:30.664
where Combat Outpost Pirelli
was in Diyala province.

681
00:46:30.871 --> 00:46:32.714
They denied my request.

682
00:46:32.873 --> 00:46:35.672
So to get there,
I'd have to hitchhike

683
00:46:35.876 --> 00:46:37.719
from Special Forces
A Team to A Team

684
00:46:37.878 --> 00:46:40.631
more than 300 miles
around the war zone.

685
00:46:42.216 --> 00:46:46.767
From an-Nasiriyah
it was to Hilla.

686
00:46:48.347 --> 00:46:52.022
From there, went to
Baghdad to area four,

687
00:46:52.226 --> 00:46:54.695
which was the secret location

688
00:46:54.895 --> 00:46:56.818
where those serious gunners

689
00:46:57.022 --> 00:47:00.151
of ODA 0-9-4 were going out
and doing missions.

690
00:47:09.326 --> 00:47:11.328
- Alex!
- What?

691
00:47:11.537 --> 00:47:13.414
- Stay out here.
- Who said?

692
00:47:14.706 --> 00:47:16.583
All clear!

693
00:47:23.882 --> 00:47:25.930
Put these guys on the roof.

694
00:47:42.609 --> 00:47:44.452
All right, step in there, Alex.

695
00:47:46.113 --> 00:47:47.581
What was that?

696
00:47:48.615 --> 00:47:50.333
- He's a free worker.
- What does he do?

697
00:47:57.332 --> 00:47:59.050
Yes.

698
00:48:15.475 --> 00:48:17.477
The one's too young.

699
00:48:17.644 --> 00:48:19.612
But the other one might
be old enough to be him.

700
00:48:19.813 --> 00:48:21.133
Do you have
a first name, Hussein?

701
00:48:21.273 --> 00:48:22.525
Robert.

702
00:48:22.733 --> 00:48:25.077
Pull those detainees
and go down out of the element.

703
00:48:25.277 --> 00:48:27.357
Have the source take a look
at both those jack-asses.

704
00:48:27.404 --> 00:48:28.872
- Okay. Hey, Bob!
- Yeah.

705
00:48:29.072 --> 00:48:30.995
I'm gonna need you and Ranger
in about 3 minutes.

706
00:48:31.199 --> 00:48:32.826
- Ali Abu...
- Bob, you move with...

707
00:48:34.494 --> 00:48:36.997
- Haruz, let's go, brother.
- Ranger

708
00:48:44.046 --> 00:48:47.926
Did you actually
plot a course in your own mind?

709
00:48:48.133 --> 00:48:51.012
If this didn't work out,
you could sense an adjust,

710
00:48:51.219 --> 00:48:52.989
and you knew somewhere
else that you could try?

711
00:48:53.013 --> 00:48:55.562
Is that what... Is that sort
of how you approached it?

712
00:48:58.518 --> 00:48:59.986
I always hope for the best.

713
00:49:00.187 --> 00:49:02.861
Um, expect the worst
and plan accordingly.

714
00:49:03.023 --> 00:49:06.323
And I always hope
that logic will prevail

715
00:49:06.526 --> 00:49:08.369
and people will... will...

716
00:49:08.528 --> 00:49:11.873
Will... will maybe have a soft spot
get what it is that I was doing,

717
00:49:12.032 --> 00:49:14.205
but, uh, no.

718
00:49:14.409 --> 00:49:18.789
From there, it was to Camp Taji.

719
00:49:30.092 --> 00:49:31.412
What's the deal
with this bad guy?

720
00:49:31.468 --> 00:49:33.596
Oh, we got
a warrant for his arrest.

721
00:49:33.804 --> 00:49:35.772
It's a Baghdad warrant.

722
00:49:35.973 --> 00:49:37.816
He was an AQI member.

723
00:49:38.016 --> 00:49:39.233
Mostly what he's wanted for

724
00:49:39.393 --> 00:49:41.942
is the murder of
other Iraqi members,

725
00:49:42.145 --> 00:49:44.147
mostly another clan.

726
00:49:44.356 --> 00:49:48.907
His tribe is very large
with I.E.D.s in this area.

727
00:49:49.069 --> 00:49:51.413
What's your name?
You're the RTO?

728
00:49:51.613 --> 00:49:52.956
- Yeah, Roger.
- And I'm Alex.

729
00:49:53.156 --> 00:49:55.156
Okay, I'm gonna be on your
hipper behind you, okay?

730
00:49:55.242 --> 00:49:56.539
Okay.

731
00:50:16.304 --> 00:50:19.023
An Arrow 2-5,
go ahead, it's traffic.

732
00:50:19.224 --> 00:50:20.976
We at this time, we
are supporting Jaguar

733
00:50:21.184 --> 00:50:22.936
on guard.

734
00:50:23.145 --> 00:50:25.614
- Check the friendlies, please.
- Checking the friendlies.

735
00:50:27.482 --> 00:50:29.951
We have six Humvees on the road.

736
00:50:39.244 --> 00:50:42.965
It's about a six
vehicle convoy, over.

737
00:51:14.780 --> 00:51:16.657
Okay.

738
00:51:28.960 --> 00:51:30.177
Okay, will do.

739
00:51:42.015 --> 00:51:45.815
The compound
that is directly above them

740
00:51:46.019 --> 00:51:48.363
to the southeast
is a hostile compound.

741
00:51:48.563 --> 00:51:50.531
They can declare
that area, copy.

742
00:51:53.151 --> 00:51:55.028
All right, go-

